# SERMON AUDIO NEVER ENTERS THIS REPOSITORY.
#
# PRIVACY.md promises a church that their audio never leaves their device. That promise
# is not conditional on the device belonging to a church — it IS the promise. A recording
# of a real congregation in a public git history breaks it in the most literal way there
# is, and "it was only for testing" repairs nothing: git remembers, and mirrors keep
# copies of what you delete.
#
# Keep the recording locally. Point the bench at it. Commit the NUMBER, never the audio.
*.wav
*.f32
*.raw
*.mp3
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.flac

# Reference transcripts are what was SAID in a real service — a sermon in plain text is
# still a recording of a congregation, and it is still theirs.
*.txt

# ...except this one.
!README.md
